  "note": "Triennial election of the county council, 1902: polled 28 May 1902 in six divisions; the other fifteen divisions (seventeen seats) were returned unopposed. The retiring member. The Banbridge Chronicle prints his first name as Patrick; the nominations give \"M. Smyth\" and the Lurgan Times list \"Michael Smith, J.P., Keady\". All three candidates Nationalists."
